# Dev done - record the delivery of apps

<!-- prism:dev-done-contract:v2 -->

Use this skill to record that one or more apps of a feature are delivered: each gets one row of
delivery evidence naming the artifact it built. It does not mark the feature shipped; a feature
whose apps are all delivered is `ready-for-qa`.

## Usage

`$dev-done [F-XXX] [app ...]`

Without app names, the apps are those the developer reports as delivered.

## Read-only preflight

When available, use:

```text
prism wiki transition-preflight F-XXX [path] --action dev-done --json
```

Accept it only with common envelope schema 1, command facts, capability version
3 and an action-specific `dev-done` surface, transition version 2, and a consistent
snapshot. The Prism version alone does not prove support. If any required fact, schema,
action, capability, or snapshot is missing or fails, fall back to direct-file checks. The
preflight is copy-only and never authorizes a write; it reports the delivery evidence as not
yet supplied, because the proposal adds it.

## Supported action

`ready-for-dev` or `in-dev` + `dev` -> the minimum of the app stages: `in-dev` + `dev` while an
app has no delivery evidence, `ready-for-qa` + `qa` once every active app has it

Resolve exactly one `knowledge/wiki/features/[F-XXX]-[slug].md` source file and
require `status: ready-for-dev` or `in-dev` with `owner: dev`. A missing, invalid, ambiguous, or
different source pair is a stop condition. So is a feature that lists a retired
app (`app-retired-in-scope`): retirement never changes scope by itself, so ask for an
explicit edit of the feature's `apps` first. From `ready-for-dev` this action also starts development.

## Evidence and confirmation

Read `knowledge/wiki/SCHEMA.md`, `knowledge/wiki/LIFECYCLE.md`, `knowledge/wiki/ACTIONS.md`, `status-board.md`, the complete feature, every declared
app-requirement page, any applicable API contract, linked context, workspace
identity, advisory state, the delivery evidence already recorded, and active `revalidation` and
`app-revalidation` domains.

Delivery evidence is an input to this action. For every app you deliver, get from the developer the
artifact, the implementation reference and the test command and result, and add one row to the
proposed feature page's `## Delivery evidence` table, in the column order
`| App | Artifact | Contract | Implementation | Tests | Basis |`:

- **Artifact**: `version:<semver>`, `build:<name>#<number>`, `image:<name>@sha256:<64 hex digits>`,
  `package:<name>@<version>` or `commit:<7 to 40 hex digits>`. Anything else is rejected
  (`artifact_reference_invalid`); the board checks the form, never that the artifact exists.
- **Contract**: `none` only when the feature has no API contract. Otherwise cite the contract as it is now,
  `F-XXX@v<version>:c1:<digest>`, exactly as `read_workspace` reports it for the contract page in
  `annotations.contract.citation`. A contract that was revised, or a row that cites `none` or another contract, is
  `contract_binding_stale`. Marking the contract `implemented` does not change its digest.
- **Implementation** and **Tests**: substantive references, such as a pull request link and a test command with its
  result. A placeholder is rejected.
- **Basis**: `checked` when you verified the references, `attested` when you could not and the approving human
  vouches for them. Say in your summary which rows are attested and that you did not verify them yourself.

Add rows only for the apps you deliver, and only for apps that are `in-dev`. Do not change or remove a row that
exists: an app with a row is delivered, and a row leaves the table only when a return archives it
(`evidence_still_active`). Ask the developer for any value you do not have; never invent or imply a delivery claim.
The connected board rejects a proposal with no new row or an invalid one with `delivery_evidence_required`,
`delivery_evidence_invalid`, `artifact_reference_invalid` or `basis_invalid` and names the problem.

For every delivered app, verify the actual artifact, implementation and test result the evidence names. A substantive
table cell, file presence, or clean lint result is not verification.

The same proposal:

- sets the feature's status and owner to the minimum over the app stages (`in-dev` + `dev` or `ready-for-qa` + `qa`;
  `app_stage_mismatch` otherwise);
- sets each delivered app's requirement page to `done`, and, when every active app is delivered, an applicable API
  contract to `implemented` (an `agreed` contract may be completed only when the evidence supports it; a `draft`
  contract blocks);
- clears the `implementation` and `tests` domains of the delivered apps in `app-revalidation`, only after fresh
  evidence, and nothing else.

Require no unresolved `revalidation` domain (`specification`, `design`, `technical-design`) and no open question owned by
`po`, `designer`, `tech-lead` or `dev`. An unreleased dependency is a warning, not a stop.

Show the complete feature, exact requirements/API, status board, and log write set. Reread the source and context
immediately before confirmation and once again after it. Only after explicit confirmation may the delivery evidence rows,
the status, the requirement and API statuses, the status board row and a `log.md` entry in the log format that the wiki
schema defines be written.

On the feature page change only the lifecycle metadata, `app-revalidation` and `## Delivery evidence`, and add no other
section heading; in a linked requirement or API contract page change only `status`.

If a multi-file write is partial, report the exact observed changes and stop for fresh recovery; no transaction is
implied. The preflight and any copied request are copy-only and never authorize a write. Decline or cancel means no
mutation. This action records delivery; it does not prove QA, a release or a deployment.

## Rules

- write-capable skill
- one row per delivered app; never rewrite a delivered row
- write current-state pages: replace superseded content in place, state rationale as a current fact and keep history in `log.md` and the records; mark each claim `**Decided:**`, `**Observed:**`, `**Proposed:**` or `**Assumed:**` (gaps stay in the Open questions table) and link the evidence of every Decided and Observed claim: the processed intake item, a record or a URL (see Evidence labels in the wiki schema)

## Output behavior

Return:

- feature and apps delivered
- the artifact recorded for each
- which rows are checked and which are attested
- pages whose status changed
- the feature's new status

## Error and stop conditions

- if the feature file does not exist, return a clean missing-feature response
- if the user wants to cancel instead of recording the delivery, stop without writing
